WEBVTT

00:02:58.038 --> 00:03:01.454
And then, you know, much later
I feel like my job as

00:03:01.454 --> 00:03:03.621
an organizational psychologist is,
you know,

00:03:03.621 --> 00:03:07.996
is to really think again about how we work
, how we lead, how we live,

00:03:08.371 --> 00:03:10.204
and to motivate other people
to do that, too.

00:03:10.454 --> 00:03:14.538
And my most frustrating experiences
as an author, as a speaker,

00:03:14.746 --> 00:03:16.704
as a researcher, as a teacher,

00:03:16.704 --> 00:03:21.704
as a consultant are always when people are
not willing to rethink assumptions

00:03:21.704 --> 00:03:23.079
that I think they ought to be questioning.

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:25.121
And so, you know, just over
the past few years,

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:29.288
the number of conversations I've had
with with founders and CEOs where

00:03:29.288 --> 00:03:31.913
I you know, I give them the best
evidence I have available.